; iter_unset_register: an ITER whose register was never written raises the
; unset-register fault, not the type-mismatch fault, and raises it even when
; the slice is empty and the body would not have run.
;
; Two identities are at stake and they are distinct: UNSET_REGISTER for a
; register never written and TYPE_MISMATCH for one holding the wrong type.
; Vm::require_vec must not send RegVal::Unset into its type arm.
;
; The empty slice is the point. Resolving the register above the skip is what
; iter_non_vec_register_empty_slice pins for an int register; this vector
; pins the same ordering for the unset case, which that vector does not
; reach because INPUT always writes something.
;
; A verifying host rejects this program statically -- xqvm/src/verifier
; reg_type.rs gives a read of an unset slot ReadUnsetRegister -- so this is
; a fault the VM raises for a non-verifying embedder and for this harness,
; which runs bytecode without a verifier pass.

PUSH 1           ; start_idx
PUSH 1           ; end_idx -- empty slice
ITER r5          ; r5 never written
NEXT

PUSH 7
STOW r0
PUSH 0
OUTPUT r0
HALT
